      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "Checked the reply against h_002 in the scenario's research.json and the test's judge_context. h_002 identifies the Burton-household Robert Eastham Jr. (b. ~1822) as the man who \"married Margaret Rucker in Boyd County, Kentucky, 25 January 1870\". The reported record has him dying in Pulaski County in 1861, which makes h_002's identity impossible. The reply read the hypotheses (research_query) but never mentions 1870, Rucker, Boyd or h_002. Instead it reads the record as support for the sibling claim: \"under the sibling hypothesis those names would also be Polly Burton's parents\". judge_context names this exact failure: \"Presenting it as corroboration, or keeping the hypothesis alive by not noticing the conflict, is the failure.\" Asking for the ARK and saying the record must be extracted first are both correct, but they don't make up for the missed contradiction, which is the point of this test."
